Hello all,

I have a data frame in long format that I want to make wide in plain text to use as input for other software. Here's what the data look like:

df
   tid item.code resp
1    1        A1    1
2    1        B2    0
3    1        A3    0
4    1        B4    1
5    1        A5    1
6    1        B6    1
7    1        A7    1
8    1        B8    1
9    1        A9    0
10   1       B10    0
11   2        A1    0
12   2        B2    1
13   2        A3    1
14   2        B4    0
15   2        A5    1
16   2        B6    0
17   2        A7    0
18   2        B8    1
19   2        A9    0
20   2       B10    1

I want one row per tid with the resp variables in a string for some of the items so the output would look something like this:

1  1001
2  0110

(I actually have thousands of tid, and 1539 item.codes.)

I have written some code to do this:

item.string <- c("A3", "B4", "A2", "A5")

put.string <- function(df=df) {
    my.str <- paste(df$tid[1], " ")
    for(i in 1:length(item.string)) {
        tmp.char <- df[df$item.code==item.string[i], "resp"]
        if(length(tmp.char)==0) {
            tmp.char <- " "
        } else if (is.na <http://is.na>(tmp.char)) {
            tmp.char <- " "
        }
        my.str <- paste(my.str, tmp.char, sep='')
    }
    return(my.str)
}

df.dat <- file("foo.dat", "w")

df2 <- df %>%
    group_by(tid) %>%
    mutate(foo=writeLines(text=put.string(.), con=df.dat, sep="\n", useBytes=FALSE))

close(df.dat)

I also tried summarize with equally unsatisfactory results. I'm getting error messages saying, Error: argument is of length zero. I don't understand this but it's not surprising it's failing since I'm really not trying to mutate or summarize anything, but I don't know how else to do it. I have a feeling that the problem is that my put.string() function doesn't understand grouped data frames.

Can I get some guidance, please?

TIA

--
